At 08 Aug 2002 00:16:38 +0100,
Bob Ham wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> 
> I was wondering if somebody could explain what the different options for
> subscriptions; exclusive, time update and real time, do?

exclusive
	allows only one connection.

time_update
	update the timestamp of the incoming event.
	if this flag is set, the queue and realtime must be set, too.
	when an event is delivered, the current time of the specified
	queue is copied to the event.  the format is depending on the
	flag realtime.

realtime
	update the real-time format if this flag is set.
	if not set, tick format is used.


